    {
      "id": "game_adc731abdc",
      "role": "follower",
      "text": "*The Eternal Champion's gaze remains locked on the brass key now half-hidden in the ledge's shadow, while Brea's mocking laughter echoes off the damp cell walls. The Nord Mage's breathing comes in ragged bursts, mixing with the distant drip of water. Something small and brown darts across the corridor floor just beyond the bars, drawn by the disturbance.*\n\n*The guard's voice booms from the corridor, followed by the heavy thud of armored boots approaching the cell.*\n\nQuiet in there! One more word and you'll get a meal of rats and gruel for a week!\n\n*The key remains tantalizingly out of reach, glinting faintly where it rests near the stone's edge. The approaching footsteps grow louder, accompanied by the metallic clink of a key ring and the scrape of leather boots on grit.*",
