    {
      "id": "game_231862f6fe",
      "role": "follower",
      "text": "*The guard's shadow stretches long across the corridor floor as he approaches, the torchlight catching the edge of his worn chainmail. A thick leather belt sags under the weight of a massive iron key ring, each key clinking softly with his measured pace. His face is lined with the fatigue of a long shift, eyes scanning the cells with bored indifference.*\n\n*The guard stops in front of the cell, resting a hand on his sword pommel.*\n\nStill kicking, are we? Thought the rats would have finished you by now.\n\n*Through the bars, the Eternal Champion can see the guard's key ring within reach of Brea's extended hand. The man leans closer, his breath smelling of sour ale and onions, unaware that his keys hang precariously close to the iron bars separating him from the prisoners.*",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
